<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_LeyboldPTM" Id="{928359f7-41f5-4b97-ac89-aed21155294b}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[TYPE ST_LeyboldPTM EXTENDS ST_PTM :
STRUCT
(*
    ST_LeyboldPTM - turbo-pump interface for Oerlikon Leybold Vacuum controllers.
    (The type keeps the historical "Leybold" name; the pump family has been sold
    under both the Leybold and the Oerlikon Leybold Vacuum brand.)

    PURPOSE
        Device-model extension of the generic ST_PTM turbo-pump archetype for the
        Oerlikon Leybold Vacuum turbo pumps used on this vacuum system. It adds the
        remote-control, motor-power, converter-temperature and temperature-warning
        signals that the TD20 / TD400 controllers and the "Mag Drive Digital" /
        "Mag Drive S" PLC interface provide, on top of the ST_PTM run, interlock,
        setpoint and state members.

    USAGE
        Published as iq_stPtm (VAR_OUTPUT) of FB_PTM_TurboDrive and
        FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital. With the serial link fitted, FB_OERLIKON_TO_PTM
        (TD20), FB_OERLIKON_TD400_TO_PTM (TD400) or the method
        FB_PTM_TurboDrive.M_Serial_IO fills the readback members from the controller
        status message; with the hard-wired interface, FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital fills
        them from its terminals. Members that carry a pytmc pragma are exported to
        EPICS ('io: i' = readback record, 'io: io' = command switch record); the
        inherited ST_PTM members are documented on ST_PTM, not here.
        The status message itself is defined in Oerlikon Leybold manual 17200048.

    OBJECTIVES
        - State for every numeric member whether it holds the controller's raw
          reply or a converted engineering value, and in which unit, so an EPICS
          or integrator consumer can scale the readback rather than guess.
        - Keep the per-controller differences visible at the declaration: several
          members are filled by more than one mapper and the mappers do not all
          apply the same scaling (see i_diPwr).
        - Leave no member undocumented, so the remote command, the power and
          temperature readbacks and the temperature-warning input are unambiguous.

    HISTORY
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header and a meaning / units comment on every member.
            Comment only: no declaration, member order or pytmc pragma change
            (audit finding #563, convention conv_321640e095c0).
        2018-10-12 / Maggie Ghaly (mghaly@slac.stanford.edu)
            Struct present from the first release of the L2SIVacuum library
            (commit 3fb2c8e).
*)
//Readbacks
    /// Rotor deceleration status: TRUE while the pump is braking / has not yet
    /// reached speed. Read from status-word bit 5 by FB_OERLIKON_TO_PTM,
    /// FB_OERLIKON_TD400_TO_PTM and FB_PTM_TurboDrive.M_Serial_IO, and from the
    /// DECEL terminal input by FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital. Unitless flag, active high.
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: DECEL;
    field: ZNAM FALSE;
    field: ONAM TRUE;
    io: i;
    '}
    i_xDecel	:	BOOL;
    /// Motor input power (PWR_RBV), engineering value truncated to a whole number.
    /// The scale depends on the mapper that fills it, because the mappers scale the
    /// same raw replies (controller current P5 in units of 0.1 A and DC-link
    /// voltage P4 in units of 0.1 V) differently:
    ///   - FB_OERLIKON_TO_PTM / FB_PTM_TurboDrive.M_Serial_IO (TD20): raw P5 * raw
    ///     P4 * 0.01, i.e. the result is in W.
    ///   - FB_OERLIKON_TD400_TO_PTM (TD400): raw P5 * raw P4 * 0.1, i.e. the result
    ///     is in units of 0.1 W, so divide by 10 to read watts.
    /// FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital does not write this member, so it stays at its
    /// initial value on the hard-wired interface. Values are truncated by
    /// LREAL_TO_DINT, so sub-unit fractions are lost.
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: PWR_RBV;
    io: i;
    '}
    i_diPwr   	:   DINT;
    /// Frequency-converter (electronics) temperature. Filled with the controller's
    /// parameter 11 (wConverterTemp_P11) verbatim by FB_OERLIKON_TO_PTM,
    /// FB_OERLIKON_TD400_TO_PTM and FB_PTM_TurboDrive.M_Serial_IO, i.e. the raw
    /// integer reply with no PLC scaling, so it is in the unit the controller uses
    /// for parameter 11 (see Oerlikon Leybold manual 17200048) - not a converted
    /// engineering value. FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital does not write it. The member has
    /// no pytmc pragma, so it carries no PV declaration of its own here.
    i_diElecTemp:	DINT;
    /// Overtemperature indication from the controller: TRUE when status-word bit 7
    /// is set. The mappers note that the manual specifies bit 7 as a temperature
    /// warning while it can behave as a fault, so treat TRUE as an overtemperature
    /// condition. Written by the serial mappers only. Unitless flag, active high.
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: OVR_TEMP;
    field: ZNAM FALSE;
    field: ONAM TRUE;
    io: i;
    '}
    i_xTempFault:	BOOL;
    /// Pump error input, wired normally closed: TRUE = no error present, FALSE =
    /// pump error or broken/unpowered loop. Assigned by FB_PTM_TurboDrive.ACT_IO
    /// from the inverted i_xFaultNC terminal input; FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital instead
    /// reports the error in i_xFault and leaves this member untouched.
    i_xNCError	:	BOOL; //Using normally closed wiring

//Controls
    /// Remote-control enable (EPICS REMOTE, io: io - command and readback). Two fill
    /// paths, depending on the interface in use:
    ///   - FB_PTM_MagDriveDigital drives it as an output to the Mag Drive terminal,
    ///     TRUE from 5 s (tofRemoteDelay) after the run command.
    ///   - FB_OERLIKON_TO_PTM, FB_OERLIKON_TD400_TO_PTM and
    ///     FB_PTM_TurboDrive.M_Serial_IO write it as the readback of status-word
    ///     bit 15 ("remote control enabled").
    /// Unitless flag, active high.
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: REMOTE;
    field: ZNAM FALSE;
    field: ONAM TRUE;
    io: io;
    '}
    q_xRemote :BOOL;
    /// Remote-control status from status-word bit 15: TRUE = the controller is under
    /// remote control. Written only by FB_PTM_TurboDrive.M_Serial_IO (the standalone
    /// serial mappers write the same bit into q_xRemote instead). No pytmc pragma,
    /// so it carries no PV declaration of its own here. Unitless flag, active high.
    i_xRemote : BOOL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>